{{~##
   The library file every generated part belongs to: the banner, the ignores, the imports and
   the `part` directives.

   `part` rather than one library per file, which is what a Dart code generator does and what
   suits this output. A part shares its library's imports, so splitting costs no per-file
   import calculation - Dart requires every file to import what it names, and working that out
   per template is a calculation with nothing to check it.

   It also means a consumer still imports one file and gets the model.
##~}}
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Generated by Tabbit. DO NOT EDIT.
//
// Changes to this file may cause incorrect behavior and will be lost if the code is
// regenerated.
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// ignore_for_file: unused_import, constant_identifier_names

import 'dart:io';
import 'dart:typed_data';

import 'tabbit/tcb_reader.dart';
{{~ if parts | array.size > 0 ~}}

{{~ for line in parts ~}}
part '{{ line }}';
{{~ end ~}}
{{~ end }}
